Z||000009||Raydar||12-24-2001||01:07 PM||||I think GM was afraid of the shock loading that the 350 and a manual tranny would impose on the body. I talked to a guy who had an 88 Formula 350. Told me the roof had started to crack at the upper rear corner of the driver's side window.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I don't think 21 MPG with the 350 is too bad. The Firebird was pretty heavy. My Formula (305 TBI, 5-speed) was 3200 lbs. The GTA has gotta be heavier. I could get 25-27 on long highway trips. In traffic I got about 16. <P>Nice ride, BTW.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000010||Formula88||12-24-2001||01:12 PM||||Probably a combination of tranny strength and body strength.  The first year for the TPI 350 (87?) you couldn't get T-Tops with a 350, either.  <P>Personally, I'd love to find a 305TPI 5-speed with T-tops.  Then put a hot 350 and probably swap in a beefier 5 or 6 speed.  That would be easiest, since it's already setup for the stick.  I'd prefer the 305 5-speed to a 350 automatic, anyway.<P>That, or find an 84 with the L69 305HO.  The last of the carbureated V8's!  I drove one of those with a 5-speed.  Lots of fun.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||bocefas||12-24-2001||01:19 PM||||I'm pretty sure that Canadian F-Bodies were offered with the 5 speed/5.7 combo...I seem to remember the reasoning being something about power to weight ratio or something...anyway, I used to have an '87 IROC with a 350 auto in in, I swapped in a five speed from a 5 liter F-body and changed the computer chip to the corvette chip, since the engines are identical, and things were SWEET.||||reg||1
Z||000012||stingant0||12-24-2001||01:53 PM||||Hummm..I remember my dad bought a GTA with a 5-spd with t-tops..He swears up and down it was a 6-spd. Don't ask...but i thought it had a 350 tpi. It was in Clarskton MI. It could have been from Canada. It was an 88 or 89..black it was awsome. I was only 6 but i still remember that thing...evil looking car for a pastor||||reg||1
Z||000013||Slammed Fiero||12-24-2001||04:30 PM||||$57 To fill the tank???<P>Fuel mileage sounds right , 17 City , 25mpg highway<P>But the tank is only 15.5 Gallons or 68.1 Liters (4.54 Liters per gallon)<P>So.... It shouldn't be more than $45 per tank of High test @ approx 68 Cents a Liter.<P>Perhaps you have a Hole in the tank. <P>As for the auto / manual tranny issue. If it's a GTA ..a Real GTA it's an Auto (700 R4), . Now if it were an Iroc it could be a 5spd L98. The only way you get a manual tranny in a GTA is with a 305 Tpi.<P>**The 5.0 liter (305 ci) engine was also available in the GTA with a 5 speed manual tranny, but this required engine deletion of the L98 and had to be special ordered directly from Pontiac** From thirdgen.org<P>As for the picture.. Unless your "Big Joe" who is a prominent member of the various trans am Forums on the net (thirdgen.org) , thats not your car. It used to be one of the opening pics on his website. I believe it's still there somewhere.(I still lurk around Third Gen pages , they make great cheap track cars)<BR>Here's Joe's page <A HREF="http://members.home.net/1989gta/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/1989gta/</A> <P>The b4c Police package Was never offered in the trans am , nor was the 1Le or other race affiliated package that would allow a L98 with a 5spd.<P>We have had a few T/a's over the year , I know about the Auto Part because my mom had a GTA but was unable to get a 5spd with the L98 , so she settled for the Auto L98. Quite a few cars out there are rebadged as "GTA"'s<BR>We traded an 84 15th aniversary TA (major perofrmance dog) for the GTA. <P>Fun Cars.<P>Jonathan McCreery<BR>||||reg||1
