Z||000016||FieroKyle||12-25-2001||12:45 AM||||So I have a question now that has to do with TPIs in manual Fieros.<P>Will a 350 TPI wreck and eat parts off my 85 GT 4 speed? Or did this just pertain to the T/A and Camaro? I am confused now.....<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">      <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000017||Groove Champion||12-25-2001||01:12 AM||||The lack of a manual in a GTA has nothing to do with the durability of the transmission. It has to do with politics at GM. They didn't want to offer a GTA with a L98 pseudo vette motor and a manual tranny for 12 grand or so less than a Vette. (Here in Canada an 88 Vette was around the 40 Grand mark) Hence the reason for the somewhat detuned vette motor. Those cars ran low 15's in the 1/4 and sat around the 7 sec mark to sixty. The Vettes were turning low 14's in the 1/4 and high 5's to sixty. When I worked for ford we ran a comparison between the 5.0ltr , Vette and GTA at the proving grounds in Arizona for car and driver. It was a lot of fun drag racing and beating these cars for a weekend. <BR>Mustang , vette , GTA , Iroc and a few others I can't remember<P><BR>That picture of the GTA Yo Sweet posted must be very old , because those tires are the originals (Worked for a while at goodyear during the 80's as well , I'm a busy guy!) Those were just about the worst tire you could get at the time , if you still have them on the car I suggest you swap to something better, for safety sake.<P>Very nice crusiers , and the L98 is a torque monster (if it is a 350 car) The majority of the GTA'sexported to Canada were 305 cars , it can be hard for an untrained eye to tell the difference between the two motors. If it is manual , as stated in other peoples messages it's not a 350 L98 , it's the 305 car. I can remember the magazine guys complaining about the lack of manual tranny in the car.<P>Well now that i have added my 2 cents.... I recently got a 90 L98 for my 87 GT 5spd  , $800 complete , 240hp motor. Should make for a nice sleeper.<P>GC.<BR>87 GT soon to be L98 350<BR>94 5.0ltr SVo side pipes , B&M ripper.  ||||reg||1
